{# THE AREAS-INDEX WIDGET LIBRARY — the five whole-page layouts the areas landing
   ships, each previewable inline, one adoptable as the landing for everyone.

   Design: areas/widgets.html in the design workspace (the graduated preset
   library, source presets/areas-index/).

   FULL-PAGE LAYOUT DIRECTIONS, NOT WIDGET COMPOSITIONS. The areas-index presets
   are five whole ways to draw the landing — a wall, a register, a map, an
   attention board, a flagship — so this library follows the graduated page's own
   mechanic: the five layouts are embedded below and a card's PREVIEW swaps the
   FULL layout inline on this page, rather than the data-widget-root framework the
   overview surface uses to compose a dashboard out of many widgets.

   ADOPT-ONLY, AND SELF-CONTAINED. The surface ships exactly these five to adopt —
   there is no compose-your-own, no "my presets". Each layout is rendered here
   from the same real rows the register reads; nothing links out to the design
   scratchboard the layouts were graduated from. "Wall of workspaces" is the
   org's shipped default; adopting another makes it the landing and retires none
   of the rest.

   THE PREVIEW IS THE PAGE'S, THE ADOPTION IS THE SERVER'S. Swapping the inline
   layout is client-side and nothing else needs to know; applying one is a real
   POST through the shell's widget endpoint, which is what lets /areas draw the
   adopted layout. Which card is Active is read off that stored row, never off the
   browser.

   NO WIDGET INDICES. The design file prints one on each preset card and in the
   register/flagship plates (AX·01, AX·P1); that is the workspace's referencing
   system and not product. See tests/Unit/Template/NoWorkshopLabelsTest.php. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Areas &middot; widget library{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {# The map-of-the-network preview is a real plate, so the library carries
       the platform's one map stylesheet, exactly as the overview does. #}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\AtlasBundle\\AtlasBundle::STYLESHEET')) }}">
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{# The library is not inside an area, so it fills the tab socket with nothing
   rather than inheriting an area strip. #}
{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">areas</a> / widget library{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Areas &middot; widget library{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Adopt one of the five layouts the areas landing ships. Preview any of them here &mdash; the real page at full size, exactly as the landing renders it &mdash; then apply it to make it the landing for everyone. <b>Wall of workspaces</b> is the org&rsquo;s shipped default; adopting another retires none of the rest.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {# Reset drops the adopted layout back to the shipped default. A real form, so
       it works with no JavaScript at all — the adoption is a stored row and only
       the server can drop it. #}
    <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_widgets_reset') }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        <button type="submit" class="tgl w-act">{{ ux_icon('shell:rotate-ccw') }} Reset to the shipped default</button>
    </form>
    <a class="cta" href="{{ path('area_index') }}">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-left') }} Back to areas</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    <div data-controller="uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets"
         data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-active-value="{{ active.id }}">

        <div class="w-galnote">{{ ux_icon('shell:search') }}<div><b>The directions are presets, not a ballot.</b> The areas index is drawn as a wall of workspaces, as an operational register, as a map of the network, as an attention board, and as a flagship portfolio. None of them became a separate screen: each is one of this surface&rsquo;s ruled presets, and adopting one makes it the landing for everyone. Areas ships these five to adopt &mdash; there is no compose-your-own here; <b>Wall of workspaces</b> is the shipped default.</div></div>

        {# THE PRESET STRIP — the five ruled layouts, in adopt-only form. A card's
           PREVIEW swaps the FULL layout inline below; APPLY adopts it. The cards
           never link out; the layouts are the [data-preset-view] blocks further
           down. #}
        <section class="w-presets">
            <h2 class="w-presethead">Start from a design</h2>
            <p class="w-presetintro">The five layouts this surface ships. Preview one to see it whole below; adopting one makes it the areas landing for everyone &mdash; it retires none of the others.</p>
            <div class="w-presetrow">
                {% for preset in presets %}
                    {% set isActive = preset.id == active.id %}
                    <div class="w-preset{{ isActive ? ' w-preset-active' : '' }}"
                         data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="card"
                         data-action="click->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets#select keydown->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets#key"
                         data-preset-id="{{ preset.id }}" data-view="{{ preset.id }}" data-name="{{ preset.label }}"
                         role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="{{ isActive ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
                        <div class="w-presettop" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="top">
                            <span class="w-presetname">{{ preset.label }}</span>
                            {% if isActive %}<span class="w-presetflag w-presetflag-active">{{ ux_icon('shell:check') }} Active</span>{% endif %}
                        </div>
                        <p class="w-presetsub">{{ preset.description }}</p>
                        <div class="w-presetmeta">
                            <span class="w-presetcount">Full areas layout</span>
                            <span class="w-presetgo" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="go">{{ isActive ? 'On your dashboard' : 'Preview' }} {{ ux_icon('shell:arrow-right') }}</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            {# THE ADOPT WRITE. Applying a layout is a stored preference, so it is a
               real POST and never a note the browser keeps to itself — this form is
               the one the preview bar's Apply presses, its action completed with
               the previewed layout's id. #}
            <form method="post" hidden
                  data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="applyForm"
                  data-url-template="{{ path('area_widgets_preset', {presetId: constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\Widget\\Model\\WidgetDom::ID_PLACEHOLDER')}) }}"
                  data-url-placeholder="{{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\Widget\\Model\\WidgetDom::ID_PLACEHOLDER') }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            </form>

            {# PREVIEWING IS CLIENT-SIDE, so with no script a card is a card and
               nothing more. Rather than pretend, the page offers the plain forms
               outright, in a <noscript> the browser only ever renders when they are
               the only way through — the same escape the shell's own library takes. #}
            <noscript>
                <div class="w-baracts w-noscriptacts">
                    {% for preset in presets %}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_widgets_preset', {presetId: preset.id}) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                            <button type="submit" class="tgl w-presetapply">{{ ux_icon('shell:layout-grid') }} Apply &ldquo;{{ preset.label }}&rdquo;</button>
                        </form>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </noscript>
        </section>

        {# THE PREVIEW BAR — rests on the adopted layout (active styling, no
           actions); previewing another fills it with the previewing status and
           the Apply / Cancel pair. It sticks under the top bar so the pair stays
           in reach while a long layout scrolls. Rendered here for a no-script
           viewer; the controller re-renders it. #}
        <div class="w-previewbar w-previewbar-active" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="bar" role="status">
            <span class="w-barstatus">{{ ux_icon('shell:check') }}<span>The areas landing shows <b>{{ active.label }}</b>. Preview any design above to see it whole, then apply it to make it the landing.</span></span>
        </div>

        {# THE INLINE PREVIEWS — each layout's FULL markup, at full size, exactly
           as the landing renders it. Only one shows at a time, toggled by the
           controller; the ADOPTED one opens visible, so a viewer with no scripting
           sees the layout their landing is actually wearing. #}
        <div>
            <div class="ax-view" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="view" data-view="wall"{{ 'wall' != active.id ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
                {{ include('@Area/area/widgets/_wall.html.twig') }}
            </div>
            <div class="ax-view" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="view" data-view="register"{{ 'register' != active.id ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
                {{ include('@Area/area/widgets/_register.html.twig') }}
            </div>
            <div class="ax-view" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="view" data-view="map"{{ 'map' != active.id ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
                {{ include('@Area/area/widgets/_map.html.twig') }}
            </div>
            <div class="ax-view" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="view" data-view="attention"{{ 'attention' != active.id ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
                {{ include('@Area/area/widgets/_attention.html.twig') }}
            </div>
            <div class="ax-view" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-presets-target="view" data-view="flagship"{{ 'flagship' != active.id ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
                {{ include('@Area/area/widgets/_flagship.html.twig') }}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
